Bard wrote:
> 
> The S. of Might causes conflict when invoked. I think the Arkenstone
> should always cause conflict when carried openly, but should also
> aggravate monster.

I like the principle of inherent negative effects with artifacts that
you incidentally suggest. Nethack already has Stormbringer that has
negative side effects, would be nice - though maybe hard to design? -
if all overly positive artifact powers have some constraining element.
The drawbacks might be as simple as reduced luck, but Bard's point of
conflict and aggravation shows that there are quite some interesting
possibilities.

One would have to carefully balance any artifacts application; would
be in the spirit of Nethack, and more interesting and challenging to
play than the "I have it, now nothing can happen to me" approach, I'd
say. At least its a new dimension how to make the game harder without
introducing new monsters or simply more damage done, and the demanding
game wouldn't affect much the first part of the game, where beginners
still have their own problems advancing.

